AB  - The paper describes the development of sugar consumption and price in the Czech Republic. The research focuses on the evaluation of absolute and relative fluctuations in sugar price and consumption. The dependence between the price and the quantity of sugar demanded and consumed is examined using regression and correlation analysis and the ARIMA model, which examines the dependence between the nominal price and the quantity consumed, as well as the real price and the quantity consumed. For the examined quantities, only the dependence between the nominal price and the consumed quantity was confirmed. The dependence between the real price and the consumed quantity was not confirmed.
