AB  - The Czech sugar market is a part of the world sugar market. Sugar production in the Czech Republic has undergone a number of changes in recent years; especially Czech accession to the European Union has changed the market significantly. These facts also reflect in the structure of foreign trade. In the long term, sugar consumption has increased leading to an increase and change of the structure of import demand; consumers now prefer cane sugar more than in the past. This paper analyzes import demand, export supply and evaluates a survey carried out among Czech residents concentrating on consumption demand.
